# expect.stdout: 7\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which does not yet recognize `start`/`await` body verbs that flow through `useRetry`/sharedState mutation. Direct semsc.py compilation is correct: `python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `7` because the synchronous `start` lowering runs the helper and the helper writes 7 into shared state before `await`. Closing means teaching bootstrap_general to alias start→run and await→no-op.
project StartAwaitSyncLowering
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main
error MainError
errorCase MainError Placeholder CSignedInt32
const zeroInitial I64 0
const sevenValue I64 7
sharedState process mutable backgroundJobResultValue I64 zeroInitial
operation backgroundJobWritesShared
input backgroundJobWritesShared trigger I64
output backgroundJobWritesShared I64
set sharedState backgroundJobResultValue sevenValue
returnValue sevenValue
operation main
input main console Console
output main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose main "start runs the helper; await is a no-op; the helper's sharedState mutation must be visible after await."
invariant main "Output is 7 (set by the helper), not 0 (the initial). If start were a true no-op, this would print 0."
label startMain
call backgroundJobCall backgroundJobWritesShared
arg backgroundJobCall trigger zeroInitial
start backgroundJobCall
await backgroundJobCall
call writeFinalCall console.writeIntegerLine
arg writeFinalCall console console
arg writeFinalCall value backgroundJobResultValue
run writeFinalCall
ignoreOk writeFinalCall Void
const successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
returnOk successfulExitCode
